valid-drop-error | A6 | error finding + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n123|| N-heads-dup | A8 Build | duplicated heads | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n124|| N-evidence-dup | A9 | duplicated (kind, blob) | `TestEvidenceOrderSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n125|| N-evidence-count | A10 | 65537 rows, both entries | `TestEvidenceCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n126|| N-findings-count-build | A10 | 4097 findings at Build | `TestFindingsCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n127|| N-findings-count-decode | A10 | 4097 findings at Decode | `TestFindingsCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n128|| N-closed-readback | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in shape | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n129|| N-closed-evidence | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in row | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n130|| N-closed-report | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in shape | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n131|| N-schema-neighbor | A2 | sibling URN as schema | `TestEnvelopeLiterals` | KILLED | KILLED |\n132|| N-version-neighbor | A2 | `2.0.0` as version | `TestEnvelopeLiterals` | KILLED | KILLED |\n133|| N-relabel-admit | A15/C13 | docs valid under the other mode | `TestModeRelabelRefused` | KILLED | KILLED |\n134|| N-parse-count-edge | A11 Build | 2^53 count | `TestScalarGates` | KILLED | KILLED |\n135|| N-control-neutral | control | nothing (comment-only) | full suite | SURVIVED | SURVIVED |\n136|| P-census-entry | A17 plant | ninth export carrying a row | `TestExportedAPIInventory` | RED | RED |\n137|| P-owner-call-removed | A17 plant | (removed owner call) | `TestOwnerReachability` | RED¹ | RED¹ |\n138|| P-forked-literal | A17 plant | re-added owner literal | `TestNoForkedLiterals` | RED | RED |\n139|| P-severity-second | A17 plant | second Severity matcher | `TestErrorSeverityDecidedOnDecodedField` | RED | RED |\n140|| P-guard-literal-list | A1 plant | 10-name literal list | `TestMemberCensusNoLiteralList` | RED | RED |\n141|\n142|¹ red via build failure (the removed call leaves the variable\n143|undefined): the pin depends on the call's presence.\n144|\n145|Kill-mechanism honesty: N-closed-*, N-schema-neighbor, and\n146|N-version-neighbor admit past the weakened gate and are then\n147|refused downstream by the identity gate; the killer fails on the\n148|changed refusal literal, which proves the weakened gate's presence\n149|and literal for the admitted member. N-valid-drop-* disagree with\n150|the spec-derived oracle (never with production), which is the kill.\n151|N-session-bound was WITHDRAWN after it survived the first battery:\n152|a single-member bound widening is masked by the sibling bound gate\n153|under the equality constraint; the edge is proven by\n154|`TestNativeSessionStringEdges` and the conjoining gate by\n155|N-identity-len. Its log rides the evidence tar under `withdrawn/`.\n156|\n157|## Importer outcome grid\n158|\n159|This leaf adds `internal/clonereadback` (new files only) and edits\n160|no landed file: the tracked tree equals the story tip (`5e40826`\n161|= trunk `6d3bff9` + the three signed story checkpoints), so the\n162|five reused owner packages are byte-identical between base and\n163|candidate and their suites are green on the candidate tree — no\n164|input class moved. The grid is keyed (package, entry, input).\n165|Base is the story tip; candidate is the uncommitted tree.\n166|\n167|| Package | Entry | Input classes through this leaf | Base | Candidate | Moved |\n168||---|---|---|---|---|---|\n169|| `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` | valid objects; dup-member / trailing-data / non-object docs | green | green | none |\n170|| `internal/environ` | `StringLength` | ASCII + multibyte at every bound | green | green | none |\n171|| `internal/environ` | `CheckStringBounds` | in-bound; over-max / under-min / non-string | green | green | none |\n172|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` | in-bound; fraction / exponent / string / 2^53 | green | green | none |\n173|| `internal/environ` | `CheckDigest` | valid sha256; malformed | green | green | none |\n174|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUUIDv7` | valid v7; v4 / malformed | green | green | none |\n175|| `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueStrings` | sorted-unique; unsorted / dup / over-count | green | green | none |\n176|| `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest` / `ParseUUIDv7` | valid; malformed | green | green | none |\n177|| `internal/scalar` | `SHA256Digest` | canonical omit-self bytes | green | green | none |\n178|| `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` | manifest / report / row objects | green | green | none |\n179|| `internal/clonebundle` | `EncodeExtensions` | closed maps; bad keys / values | green | green | none |\n180|| `internal/clonebundle` | `CheckExtensionsClosed` | closed; open / nested-dup | green | green | none |\n181|| `internal/clonebundle` | `OmitSelfDigest` | member maps + self field; tampered claims | green | green | none |\n182|| `internal/clonebundle` | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | valid bindings; broken bindings | green | green | none |\n183|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` | valid tuples; broken tuples | green | green | none |\n184|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeFindings` | valid arrays; broken rows / over-count | green | green | none |\n185|| `internal/clonereadback` | `BuildReadBackEvidenceManifest` | valid manifest; every invalid class in the clause map | n/a (new) | green | none (new surface, no importer yet) |\n186|| `internal/clonereadback` | `DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest` | sealed manifest; mutated / hand-built docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n187|| `internal/clonereadback` | `BuildValidationReport` | valid report; every invalid class incl. flipped valid | n/a (new) | green | none |\n188|| `internal/clonereadback` | `DecodeValidationReport` | sealed report; mutated / hand-built docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n189|| `internal/clonereadback` | 4 vocabulary helpers | in-vocabulary; neighbors incl. invalid UTF-8 | n/a (new) | green | none |\n190|\n191|No `internal/clonefidelity` or `internal/cloneplan` row: no entry\n192|carries their row shapes (references are digests), pinned by\n193|`TestOwnerRowCensusIsEmpty` + `TestNoOwnerImports`.\n194|\n195|## Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived)\n196|\n197|- Report \"matching tuple\" needs the read manifests' observed\n198|  tuples as cross-inputs; only the single-tuple shape is gated\n199|  here. Owned by the final reconciliation leaf.\n200|- Cross-input pairing (plan/projected/staged/live/fidelity IDs\n201|  cohere) needs the sibling inputs; digests are opaque here. Final\n202|  leaf.\n203|- `parsed_event_count` carries no stated derivation from heads or\n204|  rows; any uint53 admits. Spec-silent.\n205|- `structural_digest` carries no stated preimage; any digest\n206|  admits. Spec-silent.\n207|- Blob descriptor agreement (descriptor vs blob ID + byte count)\n208|  needs an object store; these entries take no fetch. Unverified\n209|  here by construction.\n210|- `parsed_event_count` vs `parsed_head_ids` cardinality: no stated\n211|  relation; independent bounds only.\n212|- Single-member native-ID bound narrowings are masked by the\n213|  sibling bound under the equality constraint (see mutant table);\n214|  edges proven directly.","final_result":true}}}
